Contract proof added in:

- packages/parent-domain/src/app-game-time-budget-policy-rules.ts
- packages/parent-domain/src/app-game-time-budget-policy.ts
- packages/parent-domain/tests/app-game-time-budget-policy.test.ts
- packages/parent-domain/tests/app-game-time-budget-policy-recovery.test.ts

Covered behavior:

- App and game target kinds include all-apps, specific app, app category, risk
  app, all-games, specific game, and game category targets.
- Session inputs reference stored session evidence and distinguish native app,
  native game, and launcher-game candidate sessions.
- Running-time and foreground-only duration modes remain distinct.
- Counted and excluded session references must match the session input table
  and the selected target/mode.
- Policy decisions require schedule evidence, stored session refs, and policy
  preview evidence refs.
- Bonus-time grants extend the effective budget only with approval and audit
  refs for the approved-active state.
- Dry-run decisions expose observe, warn, ask-parent, time-limit-dry-run, and
  manual-required actions without calling an adapter.
- Restart-recovered timer state requires timer refs and recovery audit refs.

Focused tests:

- uses stored app/game session summaries to count only matching targets
- keeps foreground-only and running-time modes distinct
- requires approval and audit refs before bonus time extends the limit
- keeps ask-parent and manual-required decisions in dry-run-only states
- requires timer and audit refs when restart recovery is claimed
